n><span><span>Pale Ale</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> with Chinook, Centennial &amp; Nectaron<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Hi-Wire Zirkusfest</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Marzen<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Bingo Beer Porch </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Light Lager</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/e49a91ba-d8ac-f8e2-ef02-003e5450fb3e.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🦄 Treats from </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Duclaw</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>The PastryArchy Cookies &amp; Cream </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Stout<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Sour Me Unicorn Farts</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Pink Lemonade Sour with glitter</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/36c32e33-b4ae-07f9-2044-3e68d762ae54.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🌰 Barrels for days with </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Boulevard</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Barrel Aged Variety Pack</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Cellar Key</span></span></span></span></strong></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/60f04bef-3fa9-a9dd-c111-b83da0d6e597.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🌶️ Heavy hitters from </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Adroit Theory</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>The Devil Made Me</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Smoked Porter with Serrano Peppers<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Black As Your Soul</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Russian Imperial Stout<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Antimatter</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Hazy Triple IPA with Mosaic, Citra &amp; Motueka<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>VOIID-01</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Hazy DIPA with Citra, Mosaic, Simcoe &amp; Azacca</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/da4f6ce2-46ac-f860-d297-89c695e8413f.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><img src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1f9d0/32.png\" alt=\"🧐\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"> Something for everyone</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Fair State Spirit Foul </span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>IPA with Strata &amp; Mosaic</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Bear Chase Baltic Bear</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Baltic Porter<br>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Coastal Diamonds &amp; Pearls</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Session IPA with Strata &amp; El Dorado</span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://dim.mcusercontent.com/cs/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/2c21cf21-5b9a-72e0-9a09-92a399a33b09.png?dpr=2&amp;rect=34%2C98%2C301%2C301&amp;w=229&amp;h=229\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><strong><span><span><span><span>Barrel Aged Abraxas</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> arrives tomorrow!</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/281e3c92-66f6-cf5d-ced5-74da838f38d5.jpeg\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><strong>Christian Lauverjat Moulin des Vrilleres Sancerre: </strong><span><span><span><span>A beautiful Sauvignon Blanc with notes of herbs and gooseberries plus bright citrus. Dry and crisp with great minerality, this wine is wonderfully steely.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Mas de Cabres Estive Rose</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>: </span></span></span><span><span><span><span>Situated where the Languedoc comes together with the Rhone Valley, this family estate sits on a mosaic of limestone and red clay soils. Estive is the perfect bottle to share with friends or with a personal charcuterie board. Raspberries and cherries pair with savory spice and a smooth mineral finish.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Le Ballon Rouge</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>: </span></span></span><span><span><span><span>Win, win, win with this organic French blend of Cabernet Sauvignon and Syrah. All of the fruit is fermented in concrete for deep rich fruit combined with leather and spice. Beth's new favorite weeknight red.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span>Purlieu \"Le Pich\" Napa Cabernet Sauvignon</span></span><span><span>: </span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Purlieu means \"the edge of the forest\" - a nod to the winery's under-the-radar Napa AVA of Coombsville. Sitting near the San Pablo Bay, Coombsville temps swing about 10 degrees cooler than northern Napa, which creates climate perfection for an elegant, structured Cabernet that reminds us of how Napa was a couple decades ago. Purlieu delivers everything you want from Napa in a seamless, crowd-pleasing package with a gorgeous nose of crushed blueberries, black cherry, pencil lead, and violets, followed by a full, silky palate of boysenberries, cassis, juicy plum, and milk chocolate, with plush tannins.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/c6837362-1ddb-75e9-6681-1e43bed285db.jpeg\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><span><span><span>Back when I worked as a CPA and had to pick something off a wine list under pressure, Albariño was my go-to (an unexpected choice that somehow pleased everyone at the table). It's a personal favorite of mine, holding its own against go-to whites like Pinot Grigio or Sauvignon Blanc. New to our shelf is </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Benito Santos Igrexario de Saiar Albariño</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>, a bottle that received rave reviews when it was featured in our Wine Club earlier this year.</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>When it comes to Rias Baixas and Albariño, one name looms largest: Benito Santos. He's not only credited with bringing the Albariño grape back from the brink, but he also played a key role in establishing Rias Baixas as its own DO back in the 1980s. Today, Benito's estate is run by new owners who oversee three vineyard sites in the region, each named for a nearby chapel: Saiar, Bemil, and Xoan. The Benito Santos Igrexario de Saiar Albariño comes from the Val do Saines, known locally as Saiar, where organically farmed vines (some 25 years old) grow in granite-rich soil. After a hand harvest, the grapes ferment in stainless steel before spending three months resting on the lees, a step that gives added character.</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>The Saiar Albariño had me at first whiff, with peach and white blossom aromas leaping out of the glass. On the palate, it practically pulls you toward the shoreline, layering saline minerality with bright citrus and tropical notes. That signature Albariño texture is on full display, and the time on lees gives it extra weight and structure, enough to stand up to richer dishes. That said, pair it with seafood and you've found its true soulmate.</span></span></span></p>\n<p><em><span><span><span><span>This week’s writeup is brought to you by Beth</span></span></span></span></em></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/ac2639d9-7c97-6f99-4b16-27bd4f299ef2.jpeg\" width=\"612\" alt=\"breathe11x17in_2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p>Thanks for your business! See you soon, Beth, Julie &amp; Aidan and the entire Brew Crew</p>",
